<Layout lang="en" path="/privacy" counterpart="/it/privacy" title="Website privacy | Duettino" description="What this website collects about its visitors: no cookies, no analytics, and only what GitHub Pages logs as its host.">
  <h1>Website privacy</h1>
  <p>
    This page is about this website only. For what the Duettino app does with
    your data, see the <a href="/#faq">FAQ</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    Fabio Lazzaroni, VAT number 03963600162, based in Castelcovati (BS), Italy.
    Contact: <a href="mailto:lazzaroni@jeflab.it">lazzaroni@jeflab.it</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What this website collects</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing. This website uses no cookies and no analytics, and has no forms or
    accounts. It loads nothing from other websites: fonts come from your
    system, and images and scripts are served from this site.
  </p>
  <p>
    It remembers your light or dark theme choice in your browser
    (<code>localStorage</code>) and nowhere else. The choice is never sent to
    anyone.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. According to GitHub, when a GitHub Pages
    site is visited, the visitor's IP address is logged and stored for security
    purposes, regardless of whether the visitor has signed into GitHub or not.
    How GitHub handles this data is described in the
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    Links that leave the site (GitHub, my personal website) send data to those
    sites only if you click them.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>This page may be updated as the site changes.</p>
  <p><a href="/">Back to Duettino</a></p>
</Layout>
